    "concept": "CO & Architecture - Floating-Point Consecutive Spacing",
    "markdown": "### 1. Concept Overview\nThe spacing (quantum) between adjacent floating-point numbers is determined by the weight of the least significant bit (LSB) of the significand (mantissa) scaled by the base raised to the exponent. For a fixed exponent $e$, representable numbers are uniformly spaced. As the exponent increases, the distance between successive numbers grows exponentially. The maximum difference between two successive representable real numbers occurs at the **largest valid exponent**.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Format Specification & Parameters\n* **Total width**: $16$ bits:\n  * Sign field $s$: $1$ bit.\n  * Exponent field $e$: $6$ bits ($e_5 e_4 e_3 e_2 e_1 e_0$). Bias $= 31$.\n  * Mantissa field $m$: $9$ bits ($m_8 m_7 \\dots m_0$).\n* **Value representation**:\n  $$\\text{Value} = (-1)^s \\left(1 + m \\times 2^{-9}\\right) 2^{e - 31}, \\quad \\text{for } e \\neq 111111_2$$\n  If $e = 111111_2$, the representation is reserved for $0$.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Mathematical Derivation of Consecutive Spacing\n\nFor two successive numbers with the same exponent $e$ having mantissa values $m$ and $m + 1$:\n$$\\Delta(e) = \\left[\\left(1 + (m + 1) \\times 2^{-9}\\right) 2^{e - 31}\\right] - \\left[\\left(1 + m \\times 2^{-9}\\right) 2^{e - 31}\\right]$$\n$$\\Delta(e) = 2^{-9} \\cdot 2^{e - 31} = 2^{e - 40}$$\n\nTo find the **maximum difference**, we must maximize the exponent $e$.\n* The exponent field has $6$ bits, so the maximum possible binary value is $111111_2 = 63_{10}$.\n* However, the specification explicitly excludes $e = 111111_2$ (which represents $0$).\n* Thus, the maximum allowable exponent is:\n  $$e_{\\max} = 111110_2 = 62_{10}$$\n\nSubstitute $e_{\\max} = 62$ into the step formula:\n$$\\Delta_{\\max} = 2^{62 - 40} = 2^{22}$$\n\n---\n\n### 4. Distractor Analysis\n* **Option A ($2^{-40}$)**: Incorrect. Corresponds to the minimum spacing between consecutive numbers at the smallest exponent $e = 0$ ($2^{0 - 40} = 2^{-40}$).\n* **Option B ($2^{-9}$)**: Incorrect. This is simply the resolution of the fractional mantissa field without exponent scaling ($2^{31 - 40} = 2^{-9}$ at $e = 31$).\n* **Option C ($2^{22}$)**: **Correct**. Evaluates to $2^{62 - 40} = 2^{22}$ at the maximum valid exponent $e = 62$.\n* **Option D ($2^{31}$)**: Incorrect. Represents an erroneous calculation using $e = 63$ without subtracting the 9 mantissa bits ($2^{62 - 31}$).\n\n---\n\n### 5. Concluding Answer\n**Correct Answer: (C) $2^{22}$**",
